# Manual client package - exact M0-M8 normative acceptance

## Authority and exact incorporation

Owner task PACC-PHASE6-MANUAL-PACKAGE-M0-M8-ACCEPTANCE-1 conditionally accepts exact M0-M8, subject to the16 conditions, compatibility review and official executor approval. This designated record takes effect ONLY after official executor approval of exact creation and post-write hash verification. No code/target/operational qualification or functional patch follows from this acceptance.

Accept ONLY M0-M8 from docs/integration/manual-client-package-generator-20261020/DECISION-MANUAL-PACKAGE-PROPOSED.md, whole-source SHA256 c6d731cf0ba4974379651a3f84756f62ed3104e7afa47a7e28c23fe630a21533, byte interval[605,15816), length15211, clause SHA256 74e08b07a1f15ae325e171abbccb049c1cbf84e6944e4bacfbdd4889f13ad768. The exact authoritative clause bytes are incorporated through the frozen annex [M0-M8-frozen-clause-bytes.txt](../integration/manual-package-m0-m8-acceptance-20261020/M0-M8-frozen-clause-bytes.txt), with that SAME clause hash. This source uses Windows-1252 byte0x96 in prose; the annex preserves every original byte/line ending, without UTF8 normalization. This registration is UTF8. The original proposal remains unchanged and is not promoted wholesale; its frontmatter, title and preparatory introduction are outside the accepted interval.

M3's hash-pinned metadata reference is resolved ONLY to docs/integration/complete-manual-client-package-contract-20261018/CONTRACT-PROPOSED.md, whole-source SHA256 b77ae570a47e54eb9c1be84ff35b267b447f532fa33c6d2522f259071eb60194. Incorporate ONLY the exact config.bin/issuance.bin field-definition paragraphs at byte interval[10548,12063), length1515, SHA256 69d49101d5cc66bcab214f1f63039e098114c90581d7e9d6ec94047f2517cafe, reproduced in [metadata-field-definitions-frozen.txt](../integration/manual-package-m0-m8-acceptance-20261020/metadata-field-definitions-frozen.txt). Apply M3 C1-C4 to those exact definitions. No other part of that older proposal, external-issuer suggestion, active-Session Stop-on-revoke proposal or future edit is accepted by reference. Required TLV tags remain present; issuance tag5's defined zero length for first issue is an explicit value, not permission to omit the tag.

## Delimited precedence

This record fills ONLY the previously deferred manual package crypto/KDF/encoding/bounds/trust-ceremony contract under issuer/custody clause9, the technical profile's package exclusion and the production-provisioning format gate. Earlier statements that those registrations did not accept the format remain historically true. Their texts are not altered or superseded wholesale. Existing accepted custody exception, internal CA choice, separate CA/server/client/package purposes, automatic local key custody, X509/serial profile and Principal/grants boundaries remain intact.

Historical PROPOSED/not-yet-accepted wording INSIDE incorporated M0-M8 is superseded only as to this exact normative acceptance. M8's reference to approval of a PROPOSED document refers to ordinary documentary permission; this subsequent explicit owner decision plus official registration accepts the exact M1 suite and M2/M3 format, without granting functional or operational permission. C1-C4 and canonical ZIP metadata choices are accepted as written, not inferred. M6's command examples remain proposed interfaces under its own explicit limitation; no command, dispatcher, provider, persistent delivery record or functional patch is implemented/approved by reference.

The record does not modify Browser ADRs or qualify a new importer. Browser adoption requires its own governed implementation, existing material/store/generation/reference/gate/ActiveConfiguration/lease convergence, preservation of advanced import, and target qualification. No mandatory CNG/Windows dependency is added to portable format or Browser. PapinhoTrustStore is not a Phase6 prerequisite. No second CA, root, registry, journal, worker, trust authority or PACC wire is created.

## Normative acceptance versus target readiness

Review of the16 conditions found no material conflict with accepted authorities. Condition11/section4 are enforced by explicit qualification gates, NOT a claim that current NT4/VC6/backend processing or full ED11 peak has been proved. The contract is bounded and fully parameterized; it forbids effects when target/provider/cancellation/credit proof is absent. This separation follows ADR-0034's distinction between contract approval, implementation permission, qualification and production enablement. The owner expressly requires recording adaptation gates rather than silently changing parameters or inferring compatibility from portability.

NT4_VC6_COMPATIBILITY=NOT_QUALIFIED. BearSSL source contains candidate ChaCha20/Poly1305/RSA/HMAC facilities; source/API presence is not a selected/link-qualified PBKDF2 adapter, backend artifact, real VC6 build or measured600000-iteration NT4 cancellation/latency proof. Crypto artifact/license/hash selection, standard/cross-provider vectors, full X509-purpose validation, actual import/lifetime integration, compiled transitive memory/stack and operational measurements remain prerequisites before their dependent effects. Missing proof denies use; it does not lower KDF iterations or change suite/encoding.

File bounds and the149848-byte illustrative disjoint buffer subtotal are not operational reserve or complete peak. Explicit Windows process profile3145728 and default/legacy2097152 remain unchanged; no individual quota increases. Provider/kernel UNKNOWN and ED11_TOTAL_STATUS=PARTIAL. Root/C8 I/R/A/P/CURRENT/CAS, immutable snapshots/pins, Sessions, Stop, Model E/ED08 retention and uncertainty rules remain unchanged. Positive CURRENT is PENDING_EXTERNAL_ENVIRONMENT; administrative bootstrap proof remains BLOCKED_BY_ENVIRONMENT. Active Session revocation remains POLICY_PENDING.

